From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BunkerWeb Windows port <bunkerweb-windows@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the health check port a global setting

Upstream hardcodes 127.0.0.1:6000 for the health check server (healthcheck.conf is a global Jinja template). On a
Windows Server that also runs other software the port has to be selectable, like HTTP_PORT, HTTPS_PORT and
API_HTTP_PORT already are. HEALTHCHECK_PORT defaults to 6000, so nothing changes unless it is set. bwsvc.py and bwctl.py
read the same value from variables.env.

Upstream: none yet, portable change that could be proposed to bunkerity/bunkerweb
Check: upstream's healthcheck.conf no longer contains the literal `listen 127.0.0.1:6000;` or has an equivalent setting

diff --git a/common/confs/healthcheck.conf b/common/confs/healthcheck.conf
index fe04cfe..0c3e534 100644
--- a/common/confs/healthcheck.conf
+++ b/common/confs/healthcheck.conf
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ server {
 	server_name healthcheck.bunkerweb.io;
 
 	# only listen on localhost
-	listen 127.0.0.1:6000;
+	listen 127.0.0.1:{{ HEALTHCHECK_PORT }};
 
 	# healthcheck endpoint
 	location ~ ^/healthz$ {
diff --git a/common/settings.json b/common/settings.json
index 573c919..3f6eb98 100644
--- a/common/settings.json
+++ b/common/settings.json
@@ -244,6 +244,15 @@
     "regex": "^\\d+$",
     "type": "number"
   },
+  "HEALTHCHECK_PORT": {
+    "context": "global",
+    "default": "6000",
+    "help": "Listen port number (127.0.0.1 only) of the health check server (/healthz).",
+    "id": "healthcheck-port",
+    "label": "Health check port number",
+    "regex": "^\\d+$",
+    "type": "number"
+  },
   "API_LISTEN_IP": {
     "context": "global",
     "default": "0.0.0.0",
